HOW TO USE

To run this project, run main.py. This will create a combat log file named fight_logs.csv
If you want to alter any of the input parameters (HP, AC etc.) or the number of fights that take place, alter them only in main.py
The number of fights will provide more data, but will also be more system intensive
For character statisitics, by default they are random integers within standard ranges, but they can be set to simple integers, though any values beyond the d&d 5e standards are likely to heavily skew results

Then run extract_features.py. This will convert the raw combat logs into a more interpretable table named fight_features.csv
Finally, run train_random_forest.py. This will supply the data to a random forest classifier, split 75/25 into training and testing data, then it will output a series of performance scores
The performance scores shown are the accuracy, classification report, a confusion matrix and a bar plot of feature importance
